{
 "id": "variation_credit",
 "version": "1.2.0",
 "self_load_only": true,
 "depends_on": [
  "variation_ops"
 ],
 "description": "WP2 emitter: OUTCOME-CREDITED VARIATION POLICY (improve the improver).\n\nRECURSIVE_SELF_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN_20261006.md WP2.\n\n1. Revises `variation_pick` in seeds/variation_ops.json (v1.5.0). The Program\n   reads an OPTIONAL `VariationPolicy` node. With no such node the pick is\n   byte-identical to v1.4.0 (Argmin of raw `priority`). With one:\n     * `exclude_refuted == 1` -- an op whose experiment for THIS concern key was\n       already judged `refuted` is ineligible (first-order: do not retry a\n       family that failed on the same problem);\n     * `use_credit == 1` -- each op's priority is scaled by its outcome history\n       for the concern's KIND: factor = 2*(trials - supports + 1)/(trials + 2)\n       (Laplace-smoothed failure odds; 1 with no history, <1 after supports,\n       >1 after failures). This is the second-order loop: outcomes of earlier\n       improvement attempts change how later improvement attempts are chosen.\n2. Emits seeds/variation_credit.json: the VariationPolicy node and two graph\n   rules that turn judged Experiments into VariationCredit{op, kind, trials,\n   supports} -- trials/supports are DERIVED counts over credited deltas, so\n   concurrent firings cannot race.\n\nCredit attribution needs the experiment's delta to carry `variation_op` and\n`concern_key`; reflective_faculty._compose_experiment_rule stamps both\nmechanically from the Program's verdict.\n",
 "nodes": [
  {
   "local_id": 0,
   "type": "VariationPolicy",
   "attrs": {
    "name": "outcome_credited_variation",
    "exclude_refuted": 1,
    "use_credit": 1,
    "credit_internal_exempt": 1,
    "exclude_inconclusive": 1
   }
  }
 ],
 "edges": [],
 "productions": [
  {
   "provenance": "seed:variation_credit:credited_to",
   "src": {
    "type": "SeedDelta",
    "var": "delta"
   },
   "edge_type": "credited_to",
   "tgt": {
    "type": "VariationCredit",
    "var": "cr"
   }
  }
 ],
